{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 2a16774d6c10911437fe137bd4810c01cad96b16 (tree 22327e9764c6af575dbfb0fcb8cc0880f07f52a7), SG-1 on published 189152da: the application gateway permits the exact signed session POST with `?standing=1`, and the open Lending 0.7.0 and Counter 0.8.0 presentation pins follow the changed browser bundle. The verdict binds the SG-1 implementation promise 4aaa5da0 and signs all 8 path artifacts, with packages/client/src/application-gateway.ts (7bee4bc7) first.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The 8 filed artifacts equal the 8 changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only 189152da 2a16774d`): none missing, none extra, none twice.\n- **Gate.** `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `a1233923…`) names head a4e64085 and tree d19fcb21, shows \"changed files 0\", ends \"gate passed\", and `gate.exit` reads 0 (1,337.38 s). Node 246, Counting 60, Plain 5,127 with one skipped, Native 1,240 with two skipped, crossings 0 lost, 2 stale, 0 unowned. Scale was omitted. END act 14be0ff6 matches. The review head differs from the gated commit only in the SG-1 implementation note (`git diff --name-only a4e64085 2a16774d`), so no second gate applies.\n- **Hashes.** Every distinct 64-hex value in the note matches a retained file or a retained log. The eleven log hashes (gateway, pins, native-loopback, both tsc logs, the earlier partial pins and native logs, the original failing CLI log, `run-2.log` and the gate) match the files.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (189152da) is clean with tree 22327e97. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 5. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path.\n\n## Wake rate\nNo alarm, retry or reschedule is added. The gateway change allows a request the page could already make without the query, so a session POST costs the same Durable Object request with or without `standing=1`. The wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged. The change adds no request path, so a page can reach no new Durable Object work.\n\n## Security: the gateway route\n- **Exact allowed form.** `applicationGatewayRoute` returns true for POST `/v1/scopes/{scope}/sessions?standing=1` and for the queryless POST. The condition reads `!url.search || what === \"sessions\" \u0026\u0026 url.search === \"?standing=1\"`, so the standing query is allowed on `sessions` only, with `url.search` compared to the literal string.\n- **Canonical address.** The function first requires `url.href === address`, no userinfo and no fragment, and refuses duplicate query keys. A re-encoded query changes `href`, so an encoded variant cannot match.\n- **Refusals, each in the new test.** Duplicate (`?standing=1\u0026standing=1`), encoded (`?standing=%31`, `?stand%69ng=1`, `?standing=1\u0026stand%69ng=1`), additional (`?standing=1\u0026other=1`, `?standing=1\u0026`), empty (`?standing=`), wrong value (`?standing=0`), wrong case (`?Standing=1`, `?STANDING=1`) and alternate (`?other=1`) queries. GET, HEAD, PUT and DELETE on the session path refuse. The query on `acts` and `settle` refuses. Every other POST path keeps `!url.search`. Unlisted methods fall through to false.\n- **Queryless sessions.** The queryless POST stays allowed, and the first test line asserts it.\n- **Native authority and binding.** The route check only admits the request. The native session parser and the membership gate still decide it, and the signed body is unchanged. The sandbox witness signs a request, requests standing through the native fetch, and checks `standing` equals `{ of: membership, keyState: \"active\" }`. A page learns only its own signer's membership and active key, which the signer's own key already proves.\n- **Both consumers.** The scope Worker (`packages/scope/src/worker.ts:883`) and the sandbox Worker import the same function, so one rule governs both.\n- **Seals.** The diff to `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` changes one seal, `packages/client/src/application-gateway.ts`, to `fe6ef69c…`. The CJ-1 seals and every other line stay as published. The gate's inventory stage passed with the new seal.\n\n## Presentation pins\n- **Lending 0.7.0 (open).** `examples/lending/releases/` ends at 0.6.0, and the manifest version is 0.7.0. The presentation pin moves from `69511e47…` to `c3ba4ba6…`.\n- **Counter 0.8.0 (open).** `apps/counter/releases/` ends at 0.7.0, and the manifest version is 0.8.0. The presentation pin moves from `9a046642…` to `8c4a18a5…`.\n- **Why they move.** The control logs separate the cause: CJ-1 alone reproduces its pins (`cj.log` passes), and SG-1 alone fails only on Lending's presentation (`sg.log`, expected `69511e47…`, actual `c3ba4ba6…`). The only non-test source SG-1 changes is `application-gateway.ts`. The new screen bytes therefore come only from the gateway change, as ruling ca7b5375 requires. `run-2.log` passes after both pins change, and the gate's pins stage passes.\n- **Unchanged.** The definition and semantic identifiers in both files do not change. No signed release packet changes: `git diff --name-only` lists no `releases/` path, and the signed packets (Lending 0.3.0 to 0.6.0, Counter 0.4.0 to 0.7.0, Grow 2.0.0) reproduce in the pins stage. The generated Page and OAuth module `apps/room/page/assets.ts` does not change (empty diff under `apps/room`).\n\n## Deployment\nTwo Workers import the gateway: the scope Worker (grow, lending, demo and the sandbox host) and the sandbox Worker. A deploy including this head changes both. No schema or table changes, so rollback is safe. Read the DO rate after the deploy.\n\n## Architecture\nOne condition, one literal, one table row. The edit narrows nothing that was allowed and adds one exact form.\n\n## Security\nAs above. The head adds no new origin, method or path to the gateway.\n\n## Simplification\nNothing to remove.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Stale line on landing.** The implementation note ends with \"The named security review remains pending.\" That sentence turns false when this verdict lands. Make it a notes-only follow-up before the land-now, or accept it as the record of the moment before review. Hugh's standing instruction is an accurate Status at landing, so I suggest the follow-up.\n2. **Seal comment name.** The seal comment says \"E3 permits the exact standing query\" and the note says SG-1. One name in both places helps a reader.\n3. **Shared-checkout pins.** A bare `node scripts/pins.mjs` in the shared checkout fails at the release step because the checkout lacks the workspace links for `@generalbusiness/dap-define`. The gate and the worktree runs in the evidence pass. I did not rely on that run.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7bee4bc7652ef114cd9a64764c29579a49d8d219","binding":"assigned","head":"2a16774d6c10911437fe137bd4810c01cad96b16","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d21f010b45c0ea67b67c4521f8d42de0b7d1df0f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4aaa5da05a271b90ba9d5d426457a57a6694a47a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d21f010b45c0ea67b67c4521f8d42de0b7d1df0f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}